================= Storage ================

Cloud Storage – Scalable object storage for unstructured data.

Persistent Disk – Durable block storage for Compute Engine and GKE.

Filestore – Managed file storage for applications needing shared file systems.

Archive Storage – Low-cost, long-term data storage option.

================= Databases ================

Cloud SQL – Managed MySQL, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server databases.

Cloud Spanner – Globally distributed, horizontally scalable relational database.

Firestore (Datastore mode) – Serverless NoSQL document database.

BigQuery – Serverless data warehouse with real-time analytics.

Memorystore – Managed Redis and Memcached for caching.

================= Data & Analytics ================


Pub/Sub – Messaging service for event-driven architectures.

Dataflow – Managed service for stream and batch data processing.

Dataproc – Managed Hadoop/Spark clusters for big data processing.

BigQuery ML – Build and run ML models directly inside BigQuery.

Looker – Business intelligence and data visualization platform.

================= AI & Machine Learning ================

Vertex AI – End-to-end ML platform for training, deploying, and managing models.

Cloud Vision API – Image recognition and analysis service.

Cloud Translation API – Neural-based translation across languages.

Cloud Speech-to-Text – Converts spoken words into text.

Cloud Text-to-Speech – Generates natural-sounding speech from text.

================= Networking ================

Cloud CDN – Global content delivery network for faster app delivery.

Cloud Interconnect – Dedicated/private connections to Google Cloud.

Cloud DNS – Scalable, reliable domain name system service.

================= Monitoring & DevOps ================

Cloud Logging (Operations Suite) – Centralized logging for applications and infra.

Cloud Monitoring (Operations Suite) – Metrics, dashboards, uptime checks, and alerts.

